                    briefing_text_r3:       `Design your headline counter-offer. The position must be <strong>defensible</strong> — built on capabilities Concorde lacks, not a 'AI & quantum-finance' claim you cannot deliver. Pick differentiators it <em>cannot easily copy</em>: a corporate-partner impact guarantee, a research-led curriculum, named-faculty outcomes. Then a live event fires: <strong>Concorde adds a discount and an AI module, and is poaching your lead sustainability professor</strong>. Don't match the discount — sharpen what is yours. And decide: is retaining her a cost line, or the core of your strategy? If she leaves, what is left that is inimitable?`,
                    briefing_title_r4:      `Round 4 — Defend a distinctive AND viable strategy`,
                    briefing_text_r4:       `Pitch to the board chair and an external strategy advisor. Show the <strong>capability-to-position logic</strong>, the Differentiation, Segment-fit and Resilience trajectory — and crucially, the <strong>margin bridge</strong>. A beautiful flagship that loses €2M a year fails the board's viability test. How does the distinctive offer pay for itself within the cycle — through a defensible premium price and the cost freed by what you stopped? Lay out an 18-month roadmap covering the rankings cycle and the AACSB re-accreditation visit.`,

                    r1_vrin_label:          `Which of ELBS's assets is genuinely Valuable, Rare and Inimitable (VRIN)?`,
